This directory contains a modified copy of github.com/vishvananda/netlink.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/vishvananda/netlink
  Version:   v1.3.1 (tag commit 17daef607c6442d47b0565343cf8a69f985a4cb7)
  License:   Apache License 2.0, see LICENSE in this directory.
  Copyright: the vishvananda/netlink authors.

The upstream repository has no NOTICE file. Upstream tests, testdata, CI
configuration, Makefile and cmd/ were not copied. The main module uses this
copy through a replace directive in go.mod.

Modifications by the tiredvpn authors (2026):

  nl/nl_linux.go
    getNetlinkSocket, Subscribe:
      - on bind(2) failure the socket is closed through NetlinkSocket.Close
        (the owning *os.File) instead of unix.Close(fd). The old code left the
        *os.File alive, so its GC finalizer closed the same fd number a second
        time, possibly after the number had been reused by another file. On
        Android, where bind on NETLINK_ROUTE fails with EACCES for apps, this
        aborted the process through fdsan.
      - on SetNonblock failure the fd is closed instead of leaked.

No other file was changed. When an upstream release contains an equivalent
fix, remove this directory and the replace directive.
